#: koassistant_settings_schema.lua:3149
msgid ""
"EXPERIMENTAL: Gemini, Claude (Anthropic), OpenAI, OpenRouter (Claude/GPT/"
"Gemini models), DeepSeek, Mistral, Groq, and xAI. Book tools let the AI "
"search the open book's text, read specific pages, and view the table of "
"contents, so it can ground answers in the actual book instead of guessing. "
"Requires \"Allow Text Extraction\".\n"
"\n"
"This sets whether the Tools chip in book chats starts ON or OFF; you can "
"always flip it per chat, and the AI still decides per question whether to "
"actually search.\n"
"\n"
"Predefined actions are unaffected either way; they never use tools unless "
"they explicitly offer smart retrieval. Override per book in Book Settings. "
"Work in progress; behavior may change."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant_settings_schema.lua:3160
msgid "Gather then answer"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant_settings_schema.lua:3161
msgid "Interactive"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant_settings_schema.lua:3163
msgid "Book Tools Mode: %1"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant_settings_schema.lua:3165
msgid ""
"How AI Book Tools answer.\n"
"\n"
"Gather then answer: the AI quietly collects passages from the book first, "
"then answers as a normal request: the answer streams and web search stays "
"available.\n"
"\n"
"Interactive: the original agentic loop; the AI narrates its way through "
"lookups; no streaming or web search while tools run."
msgstr ""

#: koassistant_settings_schema.lua:3169
msgid "Gather then answer (streams; recommended)"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant_settings_schema.lua:3170
msgid "Interactive agentic loop"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant_settings_schema.lua:3184
msgid "Book Tools Lookup Effort: %1"
msgstr ""

#: koassistant_settings_schema.lua:3186
msgid ""
"How much searching AI Book Tools may do per question.\n"
"\n"
"Quick: up to 4 lookups in 2 rounds, fastest, for simple factual questions.\n"
"Standard: up to 8 lookups in 4 rounds, a good balance.\n"
"Thorough: up to 16 lookups in 6 rounds, with a larger passage budget; slower "
"and costlier, for questions that need evidence from many places in the book."
msgstr ""

